Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S06
Scenario title: Vendor Meeting and Improvement Action Follow-up
Initial workflow description:
The team meets with an equipment vendor to discuss improvement ideas. After the meeting, someone summarizes the discussion and follows up on action items.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What event or condition triggers the scheduling of a vendor meeting — for example, is it calendar-based, performance-threshold-based, or initiated ad hoc by a specific role?",
      "answer": "The meeting is triggered by an improvement request or an equipment issue summary. It is not described as strictly calendar-based or threshold-based; rather, it appears to be initiated when a need for improvement discussion arises, prompting the equipment engineer to prepare an agenda and issue summary before the meeting organizer schedules it."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Which internal roles are required to attend the vendor meeting, and is there a defined role responsible for facilitating or leading it?",
      "answer": "The equipment engineer and the meeting organizer are the key internal roles involved. The equipment engineer leads the discussion of improvement options, while the meeting organizer facilitates by scheduling the meeting and recording decisions. The manager and action-item owner are also part of the broader workflow but their attendance at the meeting itself is not explicitly specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "How are discussion points and decisions captured during the meeting — for example, through free-form notes, a structured template, or a recording tool?",
      "answer": "The meeting organizer records decisions and open questions during the meeting. The output is captured as meeting notes, which feed into the meeting minutes. The specific format — whether free-form or structured template — is not specified beyond the use of a meeting notes system and a shared document repository."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "Who is responsible for creating the post-meeting summary, and is there a standard format or destination system where it must be stored or sent?",
      "answer": "I am not sure about that."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How are action items assigned and tracked after the meeting — for example, are they entered into a task management tool, sent via email, or managed through a spreadsheet?",
      "answer": "I am not sure about that."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What criteria or event marks the workflow as fully complete — for example, when all action items are closed, when a sign-off is given by a specific role, or after a defined review period?",
      "answer": "I am not sure about that."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
Return JSON with this shape:
{
  "workflow": {
    "activities": [
      {
        "id": "A1",
